WEBVTT

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.520
No way...

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:06.980
Brother?

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.650
<i>You feeling lonely, Gear?</i>

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.990
<i>I'm sad to see you going away, too.</i>

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.580
<i>But it's dangerous here,</i>

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.540
<i>and you don't want to cause 
trouble for people, do you?</i>

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.830
<i>So I have to send you somewhere safe.</i>

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:31.550
<i>There are things you have to do, 
whether you like it or not.</i>

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:34.510
<i>Someday you'll understand.</i>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:35.430
<i>See you.</i>

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:37.430
<i>Stay safe.</i>

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.760
<i>When I grow up, I'm joining the army.</i>

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.390
<i>I'm going to join the 
army and fight with you, Dad.</i>

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:49.980
<i>By the time you grow up, 
the war will be over.</i>

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.070
<i>I'll end it myself!</i>

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.450
Dad?

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:26.980
Lost Star & KID

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.360
So you're a decoy?

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:30.360
It doesn't matter.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.230
The only things past me is the prison,
 and it's a dead end.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.990
When the rest of them come back, 
I'll destroy them then.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.370
Until then...

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:43.200
I'll have my fun with you.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.540
No, you won't!

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.630
What? An exploding round?

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:53.750
Take this.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.850
What's your skin made out of?

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:06.930
Your weak weapons can't touch me.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:11.060
If my bow won't work, 
then I don't have a choice.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.780
So you're going to surrender?

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:15.570
Nope.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.240
<i>This is perfect.</i>

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:19.110
<i>I'll try it on him.</i>

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.160
<i>My new weapon...</i>

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.790
Shooting!

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:33.960
<i>No way...</i>

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:35.590
<i>It didn't work?</i>

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:41.550
Don't tell me, the reason you were so 
confident is because you had Shooting?

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.900
If it was...

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:49.270
did I just crush your pride?

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:51.900
<i>It's okay.</i>

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.520
<i>Even if our Shooting is even,</i>

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.780
<i>there are lots of things 
I'm better than him at.</i>

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.570
<i>So I'm going to win!</i>

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.170
<i>It hit him, so why didn't it work?</i>

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.710
<i>What's happening?</i>

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:20.630
I guess you don't know

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.760
that you can protect yourself 
from Shooting with Force Field.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:25.930
What?

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:28.350
It's useless.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:33.270
It'll take more than one of your 
shots to break my Force Field!

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:51.210
If you admit defeat, 
I won't continue to hurt you.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:54.710
I'd rather you be unhurt when I have fun with you.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.710
Admit defeat.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:59.920
<i>Admit defeat?</i>

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.470
<i>No way!</i>

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.720
<i>I haven't lost yet.</i>

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:09.970
There are still things 
I'm better at than you!

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.480
More exploding rounds?

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.240
It's useless.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.160
She hid?

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.030
It doesn't matter.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:30.240
No matter where you hide, 
or where you attack from,

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.500
it won't work on me.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.370
<i>It's not much of a chance, 
but there's still hope.</i>

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.500
<i>He said he could block one shot,</i>

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:42.510
<i>but if many hit him at the 
same time, it might work.</i>

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:47.090
<i>To fire a shot, I need to gather 
life energy in my fingers,</i>

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:49.510
<i>and keep it from overflowing 
until I release it.</i>

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:54.770
<i>If I could store up many shots, 
instead of just one...</i>

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.310
<i>I could maybe shoot a 
Shot several times more</i>

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:58.770
<i>powerful than a regular one.</i>

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:03.360
<i>It's all speculation, 
but I won't know until I try.</i>

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:09.370
<i>First gather the energy for one shot, 
and then more...!</i>

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:10.830
<i>I did it!</i>

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:14.370
<i>But it's really hard...</i>

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.960
<i>I can't hold it in...</i>

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.040
<i>The blood in my whole body is boiling.</i>

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:22.550
<i>My fingernails are going to tear off... 
 My fingers are about to break.</i>

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:25.050
<i>But if I make the slightest 
noise, he'll find me!</i>

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:28.550
<i>This is hard... But if I don't charge up more,</i>

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:30.010
<i>I won't be able to beat him.</i>

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.640
<i>Enough for three shots!</i>

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:33.640
<i>No!</i>

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:37.140
<i>This is it.</i>

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.560
<i>I can't hold it anymore.</i>

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:41.070
<i>I can't!</i>

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:44.400
<i>No, I can still do this!</i>

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.570
<i>I'm better at this than anyone.</i>

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:49.030
<i>I've held so much in for so long.</i>

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.450
<i>For such a long, long time.</i>

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.580
<i>So...</i>

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:57.790
<i>I can hold it in better than anybody.</i>

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.460
There you are!

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.340
Take this!

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.600
7-way Shot!

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.360
I won, somehow, but...

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:29.240
Holding it in isn't good for you.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:37.450
I've not seen my dad 
since the day we said goodbye,

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:39.870
and now he's right in front of me.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:42.130
Dad...

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:44.670
Is that you, Gear?

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:47.420
You're alive?

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:52.470
I thought you died during that attack.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:53.510
I see.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.100
I'm glad.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.220
I'm really glad.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:02.350
Sorry to interrupt this emotional reunion, 
but there's no time.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.480
We'll continue the plan.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:06.610
Right.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:07.990
We need to get him out of here.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:09.740
No, we don't.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:11.740
General Alex.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:15.200
Gear is going to absorb you.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:16.990
Is that all right?

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.620
Ramses's orders?

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.250
That's just like her. It's a good plan.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:26.090
Yeah, that's fine.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:27.500
Please do.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:30.260
We're not going to save him?

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:32.720
Absorb... what?

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.010
I told you.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:35.180
His life.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:39.100
If the general was well, 
we were to rescue him.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:44.520
But if he was hurt to the point 
where he couldn't aid in the fight,

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:48.110
you, his son, are to absorb his power.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.030
That's our plan.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.150
Wait.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:54.070
We may still be able to save him!

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:55.030
Are you stupid?

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.790
You're going to take me back like this?

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.580
Give me a break.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:02.830
If you move me, I'll die.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:04.920
No...

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.500
Just do it.

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:09.800
Absorb me already.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:13.010
To absorb someone, 
you need merely touch them.

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:17.220
If you touch them and think 
about wanting to absorb them,

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.810
and they want to give you their life,

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:22.350
you will absorb them in an instant.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.310
<i>You guys are Killers, right?</i>

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:30.030
<i>Please! Any of you! Absorb me.</i>

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:33.070
<i>You simply absorb.</i>

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:35.200
<i>Other's lives.</i>

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:39.240
<i>If you want to get better, that is.</i>

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.830
<i>I want to be stronger.</i>

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:46.500
<i>I knew that you could do 
it if you tried, brother.</i>

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.130
I can't!

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:54.170
I told you there'd be things 
you'd have to sacrifice

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:56.090
if you want to be strong.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.300
Isn't that the path you chose?

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:02.060
The strongest Killer in Segua's army.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:05.440
He's the best person 
possible to absorb.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:09.060
I want to be stronger, yes...

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.070
But not like this!

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:15.900
This isn't just to make you stronger.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:22.660
It's for Segua, and for 
General Alex himself.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:25.410
For my dad?

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:30.590
If he dies now, 
he leaves nothing behind.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:35.800
But if you absorb him, 
he will live on within you.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:41.640
Shouldn't you, his son, 
carry on his power to stop

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:44.180
his death from being meaningless?

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:48.520
I understand how insane it 
is to end your reunion

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.860
with your father like this.

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:54.610
But you understand, don't you?

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:57.570
What you really need to do right now.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.660
For Segua.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:01.830
For my dad...

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:04.620
Even if it's not what I want to do...

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.960
There are things you have to do,

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:12.000
whether you like it or not.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:16.380
Someday you'll understand.

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:24.350
There's no time, right?

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:25.980
What's stopping you?

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:28.140
I'm telling you to do it.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.650
But I...

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:33.770
<i>When this happened,</i>

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:37.530
<i>meeting my father and learning about 
the Killers was all just so sudden,</i>

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.860
<i>I felt like it was a dream.</i>

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:42.830
<i>But I knew what I had to do.</i>

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:47.660
Now that I can relax, 
I'm getting sleepy...

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:49.160
Dad!

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.210
Accept my power, Gear.

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:55.750
Gear...

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:58.090
Before I entrust everything to you,

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.010
there's something you need to know.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:05.350
Long ago, Segua had two Killers.

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:09.890
We were the Segua Army's main force and always fought on the front lines.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:12.770
We were bound by tighter bonds than anyone.

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:15.360
But one day we were badly wounded,

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:17.150
and surrounded by the 
enemy with nothing left to do

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:18.900
but wait for death.

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.610
<i>So the two of us are 
going to die together?</i>

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:25.200
<i>No, there's still a way to survive.</i>

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:30.040
<i>If one of us absorbs the 
other's life and power,</i>

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:31.500
<i>they may be able to break 
through the enemy.</i>

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:34.250
But this plan was an awful one.

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:36.250
One of us would die,

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.720
and the other would lose 
someone they cared about.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.800
We couldn't decide who would die.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.760
We couldn't decide at all...

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:51.270
So in the end we chose an insane way

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:54.270
to decide who would kill the other.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:58.150
<i>Take care of Gear for me...</i>

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:09.700
The great power I gained from absorbing 
the one I loved let me survive.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:16.000
Even after I made it home alive, 
my regrets never left me.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:19.050
The reason I sent you 
away from the battle

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:22.130
when you were young was 
because I was afraid

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.930
of having someone I 
cared about so close.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:31.140
I wanted to ensure my loved ones 
were never caught in the fight again.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:36.190
So I wanted to keep all 
of them away from me.

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:38.860
I'm a failure.

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:41.900
Even in the very end,
 I'm still making you suffer.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:44.950
I'm no father at all.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:48.200
I'm sorry, Gear.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:50.540
That's not true!

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:55.460
I was happy... I was happy 
to see you in the end.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:57.500
I was happy.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:12:59.880
Thank you.

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:03.800
<i>My dad gave me</i>

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:07.300
<i>the greatest power in the Segua Army,</i>

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:10.430
<i>and the resolve to accept whatever 
happened, no matter awful it was...</i>

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.180
<i>He gave me those things.</i>

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:32.240
My whole body feels 
numb and I can't move.

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:35.000
I hope the enemy doesn't find me.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.960
Ooh... Well, what do we have here?

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:41.460
D. Fisher bought it?

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.050
Awesome.

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:46.630
Let me go!

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:50.640
Did you kill Fisher?

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:51.720
I did.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.140
I guess the Tatoland army 
isn't that strong.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:55.350
True.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:14:01.110
You're pretty impressive, girl, 
killing that monster all by yourself.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.270
Of course...

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:06.360
It looks like you can't move now.

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:09.030
We have to ask you a lot of things.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:11.910
You're in for a lot of torture later.

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:14.870
<i>No, I can't move!</i>

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:17.920
You're hot enough that torturing 
you will be lots of fun.

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:30.340
<i>Gear...</i>

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.390
Thanks, Opal.

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:36.640
The mission is complete, Opal.

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.520
Huh? What's all this?

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:41.360
Looks like you just came 
from the prison,

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:43.520
but I don't see General Alex.

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.900
Let me guess: you came to absorb him,

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:50.160
but you freaked out and despaired 
when you saw him, right?

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:51.870
He's Boys.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:53.370
Bays's younger brother.

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:54.830
That's right.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:58.250
I'm Boys, the younger brother 
of the ultimate warrior, Bays.

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:01.790
I'm the one who defeated General Alex.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.880
And I'm the one who 
tortured him down here!

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:09.800
He never said anything, 
so I accidentally overdid it.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:11.550
But what did you think?

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:14.430
He was torn apart so badly,
 it was practically a form of art,

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.180
but he was still barely alive, right?

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:19.060
That's what makes me 
a genius at torture!

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:21.060
Tejirof, the mission's over, right?

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:21.480
Of course, I'd have 
more fun with a girl—

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:31.610
You told me when the mission was over 
I could fight all I wanted, right?

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.070
I did.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:38.120
<i>This was the birth of 
Segua's new messiah.</i>

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:47.840
I'm going to fight here until 
I've taken over Hope Fortress!

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:51.300
My, my...

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.340
I guess I'll fight a little more.

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:55.470
Nel, take care of Opal.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.140
I'll be going for a bit, too.

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:58.600
Where?

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.600
I'm going to finish things.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.600
In battle and you-know-what,

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.360
taking care of them when 
you're done is important.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:08.110
What the hell is he?

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:13.320
I can't leave my dad's body like that.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:17.370
I'm going to take over this fortress!

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:27.920
Hey, there.

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:29.920
So you made it out 
on your own after all.

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.050
Impressive.

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:33.550
Didn't have much else to do.

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:36.100
The mission succeeded.

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:37.140
Did it.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:41.100
One of ours is kicking butt inside.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:47.650
But well, I figured if you interrupted him,
 he wouldn't be able to finish.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:50.820
So I'll finish you here.

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.360
Finish me?

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:55.700
This time I won't let my guard down.

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.530
You won't get the drop on me this time.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.790
Yeah, you're strong and I 
don't want to fight you.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:06.040
I really didn't want to get serious 
in a fight I was just hired on for...

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:10.500
But if he's working that hard, 
then I think I should, too.

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:14.260
I can do anything I want, you know.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:24.810
Eh, whatever.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:25.850
I'll pass.

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.770
Looks like Tatoland lost 
this fight anyway.

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:31.820
I'll withdraw for today.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:33.240
Glad to hear it.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:36.110
If you'll leave, that makes this easy.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:38.320
I don't want to get hurt.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:40.330
Can I ask something?

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:43.580
That wall of light you used to seal me.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:44.330
What is that?

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:45.710
Oh, that?

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:47.580
That's a type of Puzzle.

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:49.500
Puzzle Magic Academy.

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.590
I learned all the 
techniques I use there.

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:55.220
If you're interested, drop by.

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:57.510
Thanks.

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:05.930
Segua wins!

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:11.020
<i>Gear's attack drove the 
enemy from Hope Fortress.</i>

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:14.320
<i>And the battle of Hope Fortress ended.</i>

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:36.050
In the end, Gear came 
to the battlefield.

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:39.800
I wanted to save him from the pain.

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:41.970
I think it's okay.

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:45.310
You did everything you could.

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:49.270
You did everything I would've 
hoped for, as well.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:51.190
You must be tired.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:54.860
Our time is over.

00:18:55.440 --> 00:19:00.780
Let's leave Segua... to our son.

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:06.330
Yeah, you're right.

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:09.290
<i>After the battle of Hope Fortress,</i>

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:13.460
<i>Segua lost its hero, General Alex,</i>

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:16.550
<i>but the whole country was excited</i>

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:19.220
<i>over the arrival of their new hero,</i>

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:22.340
<i>and their first major 
victory in a long time.</i>

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:24.350
<i>And the rumors of the 
Segua warrior who took</i>

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:27.310
<i>Hope Fortress spread over the 
whole continent in an instant.</i>

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:30.810
People called him "Blue Sonic."

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:32.810
Tatoland

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:34.570
Mister, it didn't work this time.

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:38.570
Sometimes you win, 
and sometimes you lose.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:42.320
We can retake Hope Fortress.

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:45.330
This is getting fun.

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:50.580
There's plenty more fun to be had 
on the continent of Consume.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:50.080
Ruler of Tatoland and the Legendary Invader

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:52.330
Havid Republic

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.710
Destruction is the 
beginning of creation.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.920
The die has been cast.

00:19:56.420 --> 00:20:00.420
Havid Republic Samurai CEO

00:19:56.920 --> 00:20:00.760
We will be the ones to build 
a new era: Kichou Land.

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:03.590
Ganp Federation

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:03.590
Blue Sonic?

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:06.850
I didn't know there was anyone that 
strong still on the continent.

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:14.440
Ganp Federation Wave Motion Warrior

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:14.480
If he's stronger than I am, 
I'd love to meet him.

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:16.360
Kingdom of Slovia

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:21.360
Segua? I'm not interested.

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:26.120
Kingdom of Slovia Ultimate Queen

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:26.330
The only man I want to defeat is him.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:30.870
Elil Republic

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:31.830
That's another big one 
you hunted today!

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:35.380
Are you fired up because you're
concerned about Segua?

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:37.590
You're not?

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.130
You're concerned about Segua, right?

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:41.970
You're not?

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:46.640
But you're thinking about the guy 
they call Blue Sonic, right?

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:49.640
Elil Republic Hero 

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:49.100
Yes.

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:55.020
Ninteldo Empire Gambling Hall

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:54.230
Hey, who's that guy?

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:55.850
I can't believe it!

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:59.070
And supposedly he just 
learned the rules today!

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:02.240
I'm doing great today!

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.400
Zelig?

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:04.700
Good grief.

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:07.570
You really were playing 
here, weren't you?

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:09.370
Know your role.

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:11.700
You're the general of the armies.

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:12.910
Right, right.

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:16.630
So does this mean it's 
time to get going?

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:18.420
That's the genius, General Zelig?

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:21.050
We're taking four generals?

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:22.920
Pretty gorgeous.

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:25.880
Ninteldo 6 Generals : Infinite Warrior

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:25.880
Yeah, let's go, Zelig.

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:28.140
I wouldn't underestimate them.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:30.680
Ninteldo 6 Generals: Miss Reset

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:31.140
Overconfidence brings destruction.

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:34.270
Just don't forget the words of Marcus.

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:35.980
Ninteldo Six Generals: Royal Prince

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:36.940
Ninteldo has but one goal!

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:41.070
Ninteldo Six Generals: The Man Who Solves All Mysteries

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:40.110
Guess we'll go finish this, then.

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:47.910
Hey there, hero.

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:50.700
What are you doing out here alone?

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:52.450
Playing with yourself?

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:53.950
Tejirof?

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:56.500
You're looking pretty normal, actually.

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:59.080
I thought you'd be more depressed.

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:03.170
About my dad? Not really.

00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:05.380
I was ready for it.

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:09.470
Actually, maybe I'm more happy than anything.

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:15.020
Fighting and winning made 
someone I know so happy...

00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:18.150
But I still don't really 
understand things.

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:21.480
Too much has happened at once.

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:23.030
I'm sure.

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:25.990
But that's the path you chose.

00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:27.110
Yeah.

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:30.740
Nobody will admire you just 
because you're strong.

00:22:31.280 --> 00:22:34.910
People respect the ones that 
choose the difficult path,

00:22:35.370 --> 00:22:37.370
even if they're weak.

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:41.460
<i>Stronger than anyone. Faster. Cooler.</i>

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:43.880
<i>I could never be like you.</i>

00:22:43.880 --> 00:22:47.010
<i>You really amaze me, brother,</i>

00:22:47.760 --> 00:22:50.180
<i>but I don't respect you!</i>

00:22:51.720 --> 00:22:52.850
I know.

00:22:53.510 --> 00:22:56.310
But even so... 
I'm going to keep running.

00:22:58.100 --> 00:23:00.310
To the center of the world!
